1
00:00:02,836 --> 00:00:04,076
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:04,338 --> 00:00:06,273
<i>The infected are being
killed all over the city.</i>

3
00:00:09,543 --> 00:00:10,636
RA'S: <i>I'm the one you seek.</i>

4
00:00:10,711 --> 00:00:12,612
I am Ra's al Ghul.

5
00:00:13,714 --> 00:00:15,683
<i>This man is your past...</i>

6
00:00:15,749 --> 00:00:17,547
Now, embrace your future.

7
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:21,219
(YELLING)

8
00:00:24,558 --> 00:00:26,220
RA'S: <i>Use the waters, Bruce.</i>

9
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:27,855
(COUGHS)

10
00:00:27,995 --> 00:00:30,464
PENGUIN: <i>You were the
one time I let love weaken me.</i>

11
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:32,898
<i>I want you around
as a constant reminder</i>

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,060
to never make
that mistake again.

13
00:00:35,302 --> 00:00:36,463
(SCREAMS)

14
00:00:38,739 --> 00:00:40,731
I heard about Alfred.
Is he gonna be okay?

15
00:00:40,841 --> 00:00:43,820
You don't give a damn about Alfred,
and you sure as hell don't care about me.

16
00:00:43,844 --> 00:00:44,954
I know you better than that.

17
00:00:44,978 --> 00:00:46,002
I thought you did.

18
00:00:46,079 --> 00:00:47,911
GORDON: <i>Jonathan
Crane's father made a toxin</i>

19
00:00:48,015 --> 00:00:49,881
<i>from the adrenal
glands of his victims</i>

20
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:51,418
<i>while they experienced terror.</i>

21
00:00:51,518 --> 00:00:52,611
(SCREAMING)

22
00:00:52,753 --> 00:00:54,881
- What do you want?
- I'm tired of just surviving.

23
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:56,055
I want more.

24
00:00:57,758 --> 00:00:59,056
(GLASS SHATTERS)

25
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:01,251
I'm sorry, Alfred.

26
00:01:01,361 --> 00:01:03,660
I've been trying to find
who I am for so long.

27
00:01:03,931 --> 00:01:05,229
<i>Who am I supposed to be?</i>

28
00:01:05,432 --> 00:01:06,491
Money! Now!

29
00:01:10,370 --> 00:01:12,669
ALFRED: <i>You need
to find your true north</i>

30
00:01:15,042 --> 00:01:16,042
<i>and let that guide you.</i>

31
00:01:16,176 --> 00:01:17,644
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

32
00:01:43,203 --> 00:01:45,536
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

33
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:49,775
Money! Now!

34
00:01:51,078 --> 00:01:52,273
(WOMAN EXCLAIMS)

35
00:01:58,185 --> 00:01:59,744
Hurry up. All of it!
Give me the ring.

36
00:02:04,257 --> 00:02:06,226
BRUCE: You have
one chance. Walk away.

37
00:02:09,563 --> 00:02:10,563
Who's this?

38
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:14,063
(WOMAN SCREAMING)

39
00:02:18,071 --> 00:02:20,267
(GRUNTING)

40
00:02:22,843 --> 00:02:25,335
License. I got a license.

41
00:03:12,859 --> 00:03:14,953
(SINGING) <i>Never
gonna give you up</i>

42
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:16,826
<i>Never gonna let you down</i>

43
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:20,626
<i>Never gonna run
around and desert you</i>

44
00:03:21,268 --> 00:03:23,032
<i>Never gonna make you cry</i>

45
00:03:23,103 --> 00:03:25,663
<i>Never gonna say goodbye</i>

46
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:29,176
(CROWD CHEERING)

47
00:03:33,246 --> 00:03:34,373
(CROWD GASPING)

48
00:03:34,448 --> 00:03:36,349
Nobody move!

49
00:03:38,518 --> 00:03:41,716
Jewelry, watches, wallets!

50
00:03:42,389 --> 00:03:43,666
MAN: You know
the drill. Let's go.

51
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:46,091
- We want it all.
- MAN: Let's go.

52
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:48,747
- Hey, you.
- Come on. Nice. Thank you.

53
00:03:49,663 --> 00:03:50,663
Ah.

54
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:52,256
- Jackpot.
- Let me see that.

55
00:03:52,966 --> 00:03:53,966
MAN: All the money.

56
00:03:54,568 --> 00:03:55,695
(SCOFFS)

57
00:03:55,769 --> 00:03:56,793
Cheapskate, huh?

58
00:03:57,304 --> 00:03:58,431
(WHISTLES)

59
00:03:58,605 --> 00:03:59,605
Come on.

60
00:04:00,307 --> 00:04:01,400
Excuse me.

61
00:04:03,110 --> 00:04:04,110
Hi.

62
00:04:13,453 --> 00:04:14,453
(CLICKS TONGUE)

63
00:04:19,626 --> 00:04:20,685
That's Victor Zsasz.

64
00:04:21,228 --> 00:04:22,228
I know who it is.

65
00:04:23,764 --> 00:04:24,764
What do you want?

66
00:04:25,398 --> 00:04:28,766
Oh, I was just passing
by, heard the ruckus.

67
00:04:30,637 --> 00:04:32,572
You know you can't commit
a crime in Gotham now

68
00:04:32,639 --> 00:04:34,608
without a license
from Penguin, right?

69
00:04:35,509 --> 00:04:36,602
Is that right?

70
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:41,813
Well, we just started it
so word's still getting out.

71
00:04:42,315 --> 00:04:45,308
We ain't kicking half our
take to that little creep.

72
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:50,652
Well, that's a problem.

73
00:04:51,324 --> 00:04:54,158
Maybe you ain't noticed,
but there's, uh, four of us

74
00:04:54,494 --> 00:04:55,792
and only one of you.

75
00:04:56,196 --> 00:04:58,188
- (CROWD GASPS)
- My finger!

76
00:04:59,099 --> 00:05:00,863
(MAN GROANING)

77
00:05:01,268 --> 00:05:04,636
No license, no crime.

78
00:05:05,872 --> 00:05:09,434
Now, drop the loot, and blow.

79
00:05:11,945 --> 00:05:14,676
You tell Penguin he
hasn't heard the last of this.

80
00:05:16,016 --> 00:05:17,450
GUEST: And stay out.

81
00:05:17,517 --> 00:05:18,678
(CROWD MURMURING)

82
00:05:19,352 --> 00:05:20,911
I can't thank you enough.

83
00:05:21,087 --> 00:05:23,682
Don't bother because,
you see, those guys...

84
00:05:24,925 --> 00:05:26,291
They do have a license.

85
00:05:26,693 --> 00:05:27,854
<i>Mazel tov.</i>

86
00:05:28,295 --> 00:05:30,560
(CROWD SCREAMING)

87
00:05:30,664 --> 00:05:31,664
Seriously?

88
00:05:35,302 --> 00:05:36,998
Best wedding ever.

89
00:05:45,212 --> 00:05:46,874
You know, we
appreciate all you've done.

90
00:05:48,281 --> 00:05:49,281
Do you?

91
00:05:50,984 --> 00:05:53,453
Three months ago,
following the Tetch incident,

92
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,554
this city was in flames.

93
00:05:56,056 --> 00:05:59,220
I came to you and
offered to cut crime in half,

94
00:05:59,926 --> 00:06:01,019
and I delivered.

95
00:06:02,062 --> 00:06:04,998
Violent crime is down 57%.

96
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:10,599
But now you want to,
uh, literally unionize crime.

97
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:12,696
- But we can't possibly...
- Quiet!

98
00:06:15,308 --> 00:06:16,571
(EXHALES)

99
00:06:22,482 --> 00:06:25,475
I remember when I sat
there in the mayor's chair.

100
00:06:26,987 --> 00:06:28,250
I do not envy you.

101
00:06:30,924 --> 00:06:32,290
Nor you.

102
00:06:32,459 --> 00:06:35,190
Commissioner of Police
in a city notorious for crime.

103
00:06:35,262 --> 00:06:37,026
That's why I wanna help.

104
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:38,623
But...

105
00:06:39,132 --> 00:06:42,432
We are fully aware
of all you've done.

106
00:06:42,535 --> 00:06:43,867
Are you?

107
00:06:46,172 --> 00:06:48,664
What do you think really happened
to those hordes of criminals

108
00:06:48,742 --> 00:06:50,404
who once prowled our streets?

109
00:06:50,510 --> 00:06:52,521
- I'll tell you. I hunted them down...
- No, no, no...

110
00:06:52,545 --> 00:06:54,571
I made Gotham safe.

111
00:06:55,849 --> 00:06:56,849
Me.

112
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:03,587
But this is Gotham City,
there will always be crime.

113
00:07:05,659 --> 00:07:08,823
What I'm offering is crime
in the hands of professionals

114
00:07:09,829 --> 00:07:11,627
and held to agreed-upon terms...

115
00:07:11,731 --> 00:07:13,927
From which you'll profit.

116
00:07:15,902 --> 00:07:17,029
God bless America.

117
00:07:18,571 --> 00:07:19,869
You have a choice.

118
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:24,407
An era of calm, prosperity,

119
00:07:25,879 --> 00:07:27,780
or a return to the
good old days.

120
00:07:28,581 --> 00:07:29,947
And they will return

121
00:07:30,850 --> 00:07:31,850
with a vengeance.

122
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,748
We deny everything to the press.

123
00:07:36,189 --> 00:07:37,189
Mmm.

124
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:40,856
What you need to
worry about is the GCPD.

125
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:45,087
When one of your officers finds
someone committing a crime,

126
00:07:45,865 --> 00:07:50,235
if that person has a
license, they walk away.

127
00:07:51,905 --> 00:07:54,739
Three percent each,
uh, from the take.

128
00:07:54,808 --> 00:07:56,436
Two to split between you.

129
00:07:56,509 --> 00:07:57,509
- Two and a half.
- One!

130
00:07:57,777 --> 00:08:00,008
- You...
- Yes, fine. Done.

131
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:02,147
Excellent.

132
00:08:03,683 --> 00:08:05,174
Well, if you'll excuse me,

133
00:08:05,385 --> 00:08:07,354
I have to go prepare
for the grand opening

134
00:08:07,454 --> 00:08:09,946
of my new club,
the Iceberg Lounge.

135
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:11,323
Good luck.

136
00:08:11,558 --> 00:08:14,221
Smile, gentlemen,
it's a new day.

137
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:21,961
(DOOR CREAKS)

138
00:08:29,209 --> 00:08:31,269
- Hi, Frank.
- Good morning, Jim.

139
00:08:32,145 --> 00:08:33,511
I'll get your
coffee in a second.

140
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:35,514
Sure.

141
00:08:37,050 --> 00:08:39,019
- Mornin'.
- Good morning.

142
00:08:42,555 --> 00:08:43,750
Everything okay, Frank?

143
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:45,419
Everything's fine, copper.

144
00:08:45,725 --> 00:08:46,725
I got a license.

145
00:08:48,161 --> 00:08:49,161
Penguin-approved.

146
00:08:52,732 --> 00:08:54,098
- Is that right?
- Yeah.

147
00:08:56,569 --> 00:08:57,593
(GRUNTS)

148
00:09:00,774 --> 00:09:01,935
I'll take that coffee to go.

149
00:09:08,415 --> 00:09:09,415
Come on, man.

150
00:09:10,316 --> 00:09:11,648
Hey, what the
hell are you doing?

151
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:13,811
I got... I got a license!

152
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:15,515
Yeah, and unless you shut up,

153
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:18,358
you're also gonna get a fat lip.

154
00:09:25,331 --> 00:09:26,331
We got a problem?

155
00:09:30,837 --> 00:09:32,499
HARVEY: <i>Penguin
guarantees these numbers?</i>

156
00:09:33,173 --> 00:09:35,301
PENN: <i>Mr. Cobblepot
has negotiated them</i>

157
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:37,070
with the Mayor and Commissioner.

158
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:38,437
These are damn good numbers.

159
00:09:38,745 --> 00:09:40,089
But I already heard
from the Commissioner.

160
00:09:40,113 --> 00:09:42,258
We have to play ball. What
the hell are you doing here?

161
00:09:42,282 --> 00:09:45,252
Compliance with
the licenses is key.

162
00:09:45,552 --> 00:09:48,454
Mr. Cobblepot worries
about Detective Gordon.

163
00:09:49,089 --> 00:09:50,819
- He has a history.
- My men

164
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:52,415
will honor the licenses.

165
00:09:52,559 --> 00:09:55,620
You let me worry about Gordon.
Now get the hell out of my office.

166
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,093
(SCOFFS)

167
00:10:04,437 --> 00:10:06,872
- Who was that?
- A, uh, dung beetle.

168
00:10:08,274 --> 00:10:09,274
What's up?

169
00:10:09,943 --> 00:10:12,742
I pulled this off of some guy

170
00:10:12,812 --> 00:10:14,280
robbing my corner bar.

171
00:10:14,781 --> 00:10:16,044
You're a homicide detective.

172
00:10:16,483 --> 00:10:18,884
Isn't a stick-up a little JV?

173
00:10:19,052 --> 00:10:21,317
I'm a cop. I see
a crime, I stop it.

174
00:10:21,554 --> 00:10:23,432
This is the second one
of these I've come across,

175
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:25,482
- and I'm not the only one.
- Yeah.

176
00:10:26,659 --> 00:10:27,659
Harvey.

177
00:10:28,661 --> 00:10:30,254
Harvey, we
cannot let this slide.

178
00:10:31,764 --> 00:10:33,426
Word's come down
from the Commissioner,

179
00:10:34,801 --> 00:10:37,464
you find someone with
one of those, they walk.

180
00:10:37,537 --> 00:10:39,096
And before you get
on your high horse,

181
00:10:39,172 --> 00:10:41,539
three months ago, this
city was in a tailspin.

182
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:44,941
We survived because Penguin
took control of the underworld.

183
00:10:45,044 --> 00:10:46,644
I'm not giving this
city over to Penguin.

184
00:10:46,713 --> 00:10:47,923
I don't care what the
Commissioner says.

185
00:10:47,947 --> 00:10:49,125
What about your
fellow cops, huh?

186
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:51,050
The past month, how
many have been shot? None.

187
00:10:51,151 --> 00:10:52,151
I know the stats.

188
00:10:52,552 --> 00:10:54,953
Jim, we will bust Penguin
one day, I promise you.

189
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:58,450
But this city has to get
back on her feet, please?

190
00:10:58,791 --> 00:10:59,791
Harvey, I get that,

191
00:11:00,827 --> 00:11:03,228
but every day the citizens
of Gotham look to Penguin

192
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:05,230
and not the GCPD
to keep them safe,

193
00:11:05,532 --> 00:11:07,172
the harder it's gonna
be to win them back.

194
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,668
You want people to trust cops,

195
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:12,669
there are better ways of doing
it than spitting in Penguin's eyes.

196
00:11:13,506 --> 00:11:14,667
You see one of these,

197
00:11:15,475 --> 00:11:16,475
you walk.

198
00:11:31,624 --> 00:11:32,624
ALFRED: Bloody Penguin.

199
00:11:33,226 --> 00:11:35,286
There must be some way
we can turn this against him.

200
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:38,559
Just stop. Stop, right there.

201
00:11:39,032 --> 00:11:40,762
How does this fit
into what we're doing?

202
00:11:42,902 --> 00:11:45,201
What was the initial reason
that you popped on that mask,

203
00:11:45,271 --> 00:11:46,271
and you went out there?

204
00:11:46,839 --> 00:11:49,434
We agreed that I have to be
ready for when Ra's al Ghul returns.

205
00:11:50,510 --> 00:11:52,855
You yourself said there's no
substitute for real world encounters.

206
00:11:52,879 --> 00:11:56,043
But my point is, if that is our
mission, we must hold to it.

207
00:11:58,718 --> 00:12:00,880
My finger was on the
button that released the virus.

208
00:12:02,722 --> 00:12:04,282
- Oh, I see.
- I know I didn't press it,

209
00:12:04,357 --> 00:12:05,957
but I feel responsible
for what happened.

210
00:12:07,427 --> 00:12:09,672
And more than that, I can make
a difference in Gotham, Alfred.

211
00:12:09,696 --> 00:12:11,562
- I know I can.
- And that is what we call

212
00:12:11,664 --> 00:12:13,826
"mission creep," Master Bruce.

213
00:12:15,034 --> 00:12:17,435
You're trying to achieve
not one but two objectives.

214
00:12:18,738 --> 00:12:21,264
So, go on then, which
one is your priority?

215
00:12:24,844 --> 00:12:26,244
It's messy, sir.

216
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:29,414
It's dangerous.

217
00:12:30,583 --> 00:12:31,583
I hear you, Alfred,

218
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:37,182
but I can prepare myself for
Ra's, and make Gotham safer.

219
00:12:40,059 --> 00:12:41,059
You have to trust me.

220
00:12:46,332 --> 00:12:49,268
(DOOR CLOSES)

221
00:12:50,637 --> 00:12:52,281
MAN: (OVER P.A.) <i>All
inmates, this is your last call.</i>

222
00:12:52,305 --> 00:12:54,797
<i>In five minutes, be sure to
make your way to your door.</i>

223
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:00,341
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

224
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:02,447
This way.

225
00:13:03,116 --> 00:13:04,277
Hey, Warden Reed.

226
00:13:06,152 --> 00:13:07,313
Warden Reed's the boss here.

227
00:13:12,859 --> 00:13:14,452
(HUMMING OFF-KEY)

228
00:13:18,064 --> 00:13:19,157
(INMATE WHISTLING)

229
00:13:19,499 --> 00:13:21,058
(LAUGHS MANIACALLY)

230
00:13:23,736 --> 00:13:25,602
(SCREECHING)

231
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:29,670
- Where is he?
- This way.

232
00:13:32,078 --> 00:13:34,638
(MAN GRUNTING)

233
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:37,006
Back when I was
an orderly in here,

234
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:40,586
he'd always talk about his
dad, and this formula he'd made.

235
00:13:40,987 --> 00:13:44,549
Some sort of scare juice.
Made you see your greatest fear.

236
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:45,737
When we get a hold of that,

237
00:13:46,326 --> 00:13:48,693
we don't got to worry
about Zsasz or Penguin,

238
00:13:49,962 --> 00:13:50,962
or nobody.

239
00:13:52,732 --> 00:13:54,030
What's wrong with him, anyway?

240
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:57,001
The toxin his father
injected him with

241
00:13:57,403 --> 00:13:59,702
overloaded Jonathan's
fear response.

242
00:13:59,972 --> 00:14:03,670
His mind created a
sort of bogeyman figure

243
00:14:03,743 --> 00:14:05,712
and now it haunts him.

244
00:14:07,013 --> 00:14:11,815
I find it very useful
for controlling him.

245
00:14:17,357 --> 00:14:19,383
Jonathan, you're
going with these men.

246
00:14:21,627 --> 00:14:24,773
- What? Wait, where are you taking me?
- Just wanna give someone a little scare.

247
00:14:24,797 --> 00:14:25,797
Excellent.

248
00:14:40,012 --> 00:14:42,140
(BIRD SQUAWKING)

249
00:14:55,595 --> 00:14:57,235
(PANTING) Yeah,
that's all my dad's stuff.

250
00:14:57,296 --> 00:14:59,390
But, look, I can't be
here after dark, please.

251
00:14:59,465 --> 00:15:01,127
I really... I cannot
be here after...

252
00:15:03,136 --> 00:15:05,367
You were your daddy's
little assistant, weren't you?

253
00:15:05,438 --> 00:15:07,202
You helped with the experiments.

254
00:15:07,273 --> 00:15:08,969
Some, but I don't
know everything.

255
00:15:09,208 --> 00:15:11,040
Now you're gonna take
your daddy's notebooks,

256
00:15:11,144 --> 00:15:13,306
and make as much of
that fear juice as I say.

257
00:15:14,213 --> 00:15:15,374
And so you don't get lonely,

258
00:15:15,815 --> 00:15:17,579
the boys here
brought you a friend.

259
00:15:18,050 --> 00:15:19,050
CRANE: No.

260
00:15:19,585 --> 00:15:21,053
(SCREAMS) No! Stop!

261
00:15:21,521 --> 00:15:23,114
No, you don't understand! Stop!

262
00:15:24,390 --> 00:15:25,790
No, you don't understand!

263
00:15:32,031 --> 00:15:33,624
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

264
00:15:36,068 --> 00:15:38,196
Good morning,
ladies and gentlemen.

265
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:41,301
May I have your
attention, please?

266
00:15:41,574 --> 00:15:43,770
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

267
00:15:43,976 --> 00:15:45,444
All the money, now!

268
00:15:46,546 --> 00:15:48,071
Give it to me! All of it!

269
00:15:48,915 --> 00:15:51,146
Hey, you have a license?

270
00:15:52,485 --> 00:15:53,919
(SCREAMS)

271
00:15:56,355 --> 00:15:57,846
Look at me.

272
00:15:58,658 --> 00:16:00,251
(SCREAMS)

273
00:16:00,693 --> 00:16:02,423
(ROARING)

274
00:16:06,365 --> 00:16:07,924
(SIREN WAILS)

275
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:09,363
(POLICE RADIO CHATTER)

276
00:16:09,469 --> 00:16:11,097
MAN: Fiery demons. Demons.

277
00:16:11,871 --> 00:16:12,871
Fiery demons, demons.

278
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:14,838
Demons, yeah. We'll catch 'em.

279
00:16:14,941 --> 00:16:17,103
- Get him out of here. Go, go, go.
- Fiery demon.

280
00:16:19,612 --> 00:16:20,612
Hey.

281
00:16:21,848 --> 00:16:23,578
Did Penguin issue
a license for this?

282
00:16:23,649 --> 00:16:24,649
Why are you asking me?

283
00:16:26,519 --> 00:16:27,748
Best of my knowledge, no.

284
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:30,354
Then why do something so public

285
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:32,496
unless you're trying to
send Penguin a message?

286
00:16:32,625 --> 00:16:35,493
I hope the message was, "Please
send Victor Zsasz down here to kill me."

287
00:16:35,595 --> 00:16:37,275
Because that's exactly
what's gonna happen.

288
00:16:37,363 --> 00:16:38,991
- Not if I find them first.
- Hey.

289
00:16:39,332 --> 00:16:41,528
You asked me to stop
busting crooks with licenses.

290
00:16:42,201 --> 00:16:43,499
This gang didn't have a license.

291
00:16:43,603 --> 00:16:45,163
And you're gonna
find them before Zsasz

292
00:16:45,371 --> 00:16:47,340
just to prove that
GCPD still matters?

293
00:16:47,807 --> 00:16:49,318
That's not thumbing
your nose at Penguin?

294
00:16:49,342 --> 00:16:51,334
- Fire me.
- Hey, don't tempt me.

295
00:16:54,580 --> 00:16:55,673
You got a lead?

296
00:16:57,383 --> 00:16:58,823
The victims, the
way they're acting,

297
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:02,310
their terror reminds
me of Crane's formula.

298
00:17:02,822 --> 00:17:04,552
You think someone's
using the fear juice?

299
00:17:05,057 --> 00:17:06,685
It ain't him, he's
dead, remember,

300
00:17:06,759 --> 00:17:08,819
not that that matters
much in this town anymore.

301
00:17:09,829 --> 00:17:12,094
He's dead, his son isn't.

302
00:17:14,934 --> 00:17:17,927
REED: Jonathan
Crane's condition is fragile.

303
00:17:18,204 --> 00:17:20,036
I'm afraid he can't see anyone,

304
00:17:20,573 --> 00:17:23,543
certainly not the two
men who killed his father.

305
00:17:24,477 --> 00:17:27,345
Yeah, so, uh, how many
loonies you got in this joint?

306
00:17:27,513 --> 00:17:30,677
Four hundred and thirty-six
total. We mustn't call them loonies.

307
00:17:31,217 --> 00:17:32,217
Of course not.

308
00:17:32,552 --> 00:17:33,713
(DOOR BUZZES)

309
00:17:34,754 --> 00:17:37,019
How about staff that
had access to Crane?

310
00:17:38,224 --> 00:17:39,590
Any of them not
show up for work?

311
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:42,654
All present and accounted for.

312
00:17:43,429 --> 00:17:45,364
- You don't wanna check?
- I don't need to.

313
00:17:45,531 --> 00:17:47,693
See, that's impressive,
'cause I run a precinct

314
00:17:47,767 --> 00:17:50,168
and if half of my cops didn't
show up, I'd be none the wiser.

315
00:17:50,269 --> 00:17:52,363
- It's true. He wouldn't.
- Clearly we have

316
00:17:52,605 --> 00:17:54,938
different professional
standards.

317
00:17:56,642 --> 00:17:57,735
(EXHALES SOFTLY)

318
00:17:58,878 --> 00:18:01,780
Jonathan Crane's
father created a toxin

319
00:18:01,881 --> 00:18:04,316
that makes people
see their greatest fear.

320
00:18:05,484 --> 00:18:07,214
This morning, it was
used to rob a bank.

321
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:09,213
How is that my problem?

322
00:18:09,388 --> 00:18:10,708
HARVEY: Let me
explain it to you.

323
00:18:11,257 --> 00:18:15,251
See, whoever robbed the
bank, they challenged Penguin,

324
00:18:16,162 --> 00:18:19,792
and all we have to do is tell
Penguin that you're involved,

325
00:18:20,066 --> 00:18:22,934
and he'll send Victor Zsasz
down here to talk to you.

326
00:18:23,135 --> 00:18:24,569
Jim, how would
you describe Victor?

327
00:18:24,670 --> 00:18:25,763
Victor Zsasz...

328
00:18:27,239 --> 00:18:28,969
A homicidal maniac and sadist.

329
00:18:29,075 --> 00:18:30,941
A homicidal maniac and sadist

330
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:33,909
of the highest
professional standards.

331
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:38,908
So you can talk with us here
and now or you can talk to Victor.

332
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:44,090
They threatened
me. I had no choice.

333
00:18:44,557 --> 00:18:46,287
We want a name, putz.

334
00:18:50,930 --> 00:18:53,092
HARVEY: I knew it
rang a bell. Grady Harris.

335
00:18:53,666 --> 00:18:56,966
Ran a crew a few years back.
Him and his cousin Merton.

336
00:18:57,169 --> 00:18:59,104
Couple of cowboys
from the sticks.

337
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:04,809
Grady!

338
00:19:06,045 --> 00:19:07,343
GCPD!

339
00:19:13,886 --> 00:19:15,013
GCPD!

340
00:19:16,055 --> 00:19:17,216
(GORDON GROANS)

341
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:19,049
(HARVEY GROANS)

342
00:19:19,859 --> 00:19:24,194
Well, well. Look at
what we got here.

343
00:19:29,535 --> 00:19:30,628
What's wrong with you pigs?

344
00:19:30,970 --> 00:19:32,700
Harassing honest
fellows like us,

345
00:19:32,805 --> 00:19:34,774
when there's real
criminals out there.

346
00:19:35,007 --> 00:19:37,875
You robbed a bank in broad daylight.
That don't make you a criminal?

347
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:41,547
I'm an outlaw.
Outlaws have a code.

348
00:19:41,647 --> 00:19:42,647
(GRUNTS)

349
00:19:42,715 --> 00:19:44,616
Criminals, they'll
take everything.

350
00:19:44,684 --> 00:19:46,118
They'll take a man's livelihood.

351
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:49,314
Like the Penguin
and his licenses.

352
00:19:50,289 --> 00:19:51,882
But we're gonna
show him, you'll see.

353
00:19:53,559 --> 00:19:56,393
Penguin wouldn't give you
a license if you begged him

354
00:19:56,495 --> 00:19:58,657
till the cows came
home, you stupid hick.

355
00:19:59,699 --> 00:20:03,101
You're lucky I'm not the
Penguin. He'd gut you right here.

356
00:20:03,536 --> 00:20:04,697
We're better than them!

357
00:20:05,438 --> 00:20:06,438
Take care.

358
00:20:07,006 --> 00:20:08,006
Pigs.

359
00:20:08,107 --> 00:20:09,336
(CHUCKLES)

360
00:20:11,277 --> 00:20:12,745
(LOCK CLICKS)

361
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:15,748
(DOG BARKING IN DISTANCE)

362
00:20:19,085 --> 00:20:21,577
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

363
00:20:21,921 --> 00:20:22,921
Hey, check it out.

364
00:20:26,726 --> 00:20:27,726
MAN: Babe, lost?

365
00:20:29,261 --> 00:20:30,422
Ooh.

366
00:20:30,563 --> 00:20:31,563
Looking for company?

367
00:20:32,098 --> 00:20:33,589
(MEN MURMURING)

368
00:20:34,734 --> 00:20:36,532
She all by herself.

369
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:45,172
Just let me go, okay?

370
00:20:45,578 --> 00:20:46,578
Not a chance.

371
00:20:49,381 --> 00:20:50,542
Don't say I didn't warn you.

372
00:20:51,350 --> 00:20:54,912
- (WHIP CRACKS)
- (MEN GRUNTING)

373
00:21:11,303 --> 00:21:12,498
(GRUNTING)

374
00:21:14,573 --> 00:21:16,893
Don't turn your back on a guy
unless you're sure he's down.

375
00:21:17,743 --> 00:21:18,767
(PANTING)

376
00:21:19,578 --> 00:21:20,578
Otherwise, not bad.

377
00:21:21,747 --> 00:21:23,027
Does this mean we can get pizza?

378
00:21:30,256 --> 00:21:31,256
(GRUNTS)

379
00:21:34,226 --> 00:21:36,286
I'm just saying, you
steal my pepperoni again,

380
00:21:36,395 --> 00:21:38,421
- I'll break your fingers.
- So you're saying,

381
00:21:38,664 --> 00:21:40,633
do steal your pepperoni again.

382
00:21:43,903 --> 00:21:44,903
I come in peace.

383
00:21:46,672 --> 00:21:49,403
You ladies were not
easy to track down.

384
00:21:50,743 --> 00:21:53,736
Then again, I can see
why you don't advertise.

385
00:21:55,347 --> 00:21:56,975
Didn't you used to be rich?

386
00:21:57,183 --> 00:21:58,811
That was before your
boss stole my club.

387
00:21:59,418 --> 00:22:02,411
Well, you murdered his mom

388
00:22:03,189 --> 00:22:04,189
and tried to kill him.

389
00:22:04,857 --> 00:22:07,326
So, call it even?

390
00:22:07,793 --> 00:22:08,993
Is there a reason you're here?

391
00:22:13,199 --> 00:22:14,199
Know about these?

392
00:22:16,902 --> 00:22:18,894
The boss can't have you
operating on your own.

393
00:22:20,406 --> 00:22:22,534
Now, he could just kill you,

394
00:22:23,175 --> 00:22:27,169
but he figures it's time to
let bygones be bygones.

395
00:22:27,479 --> 00:22:28,479
How big of him.

396
00:22:30,049 --> 00:22:31,813
Tomorrow night's the
opening of his club,

397
00:22:32,251 --> 00:22:35,221
come by, kiss the ring,

398
00:22:35,988 --> 00:22:37,047
get your license.

399
00:22:38,691 --> 00:22:39,954
Is that pepperoni?

400
00:22:45,631 --> 00:22:46,631
Goes without saying,

401
00:22:46,999 --> 00:22:50,663
this is one of those
"or else" kinda deals.

402
00:22:54,874 --> 00:22:55,874
Later.

403
00:22:57,309 --> 00:22:59,301
- We got to find a new place.
- Why?

404
00:22:59,378 --> 00:23:01,210
If we join Penguin, we
can at least get work.

405
00:23:02,481 --> 00:23:04,416
I came to you because
I wanted to move up.

406
00:23:04,650 --> 00:23:06,243
And look around,

407
00:23:07,186 --> 00:23:08,279
we're barely making it.

408
00:23:10,289 --> 00:23:11,348
I'm not working for him.

409
00:23:12,558 --> 00:23:13,558
Now, pack.

410
00:23:24,737 --> 00:23:25,737
BRUCE: Detective Gordon.

411
00:23:27,573 --> 00:23:28,700
Bruce.

412
00:23:31,810 --> 00:23:32,810
I didn't hear you.

413
00:23:33,312 --> 00:23:34,312
What happened?

414
00:23:36,048 --> 00:23:38,745
Ah. Nothing. Harvey and
I were tracking a gang.

415
00:23:38,851 --> 00:23:40,183
We let ourselves get surprised.

416
00:23:40,352 --> 00:23:41,392
What brings you down here?

417
00:23:41,887 --> 00:23:43,327
I found this when
I was in the city.

418
00:23:44,390 --> 00:23:45,630
Wasn't sure what to do with it.

419
00:23:46,258 --> 00:23:47,886
One of Penguin's licenses.

420
00:23:48,127 --> 00:23:49,425
Apparently, crime is legal now.

421
00:23:49,628 --> 00:23:50,960
And you're going
along with that?

422
00:23:51,230 --> 00:23:52,230
Not really.

423
00:23:55,134 --> 00:23:56,534
There's a number on the license.

424
00:23:57,403 --> 00:23:59,770
I was thinking Penguin must
have some sort of master list.

425
00:24:00,472 --> 00:24:03,135
Connecting the crime and
the criminal to the license issue.

426
00:24:03,242 --> 00:24:05,871
List like that would tell you not
only who committed that crime,

427
00:24:07,146 --> 00:24:08,808
but crimes that haven't
even happened yet.

428
00:24:10,416 --> 00:24:11,645
Unfortunately, the judges

429
00:24:11,750 --> 00:24:13,116
are going along
with the licenses,

430
00:24:13,519 --> 00:24:14,578
and trying to track down

431
00:24:14,653 --> 00:24:16,485
who in Penguin's
organization keeps the list

432
00:24:17,289 --> 00:24:18,489
would set off too many alarms.

433
00:24:21,126 --> 00:24:22,126
I see.

434
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:26,297
But you haven't given up.

435
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:29,931
You just said you were
out tracking a gang.

436
00:24:30,002 --> 00:24:31,026
It's different.

437
00:24:31,337 --> 00:24:32,498
This gang isn't licensed.

438
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:37,208
But Penguin will come after
them, if he hasn't already,

439
00:24:37,509 --> 00:24:38,533
and when he catches them,

440
00:24:39,278 --> 00:24:41,907
it'll be more proof that
Gotham doesn't need the GCPD.

441
00:24:43,949 --> 00:24:45,076
Sorry, it's been a long day.

442
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:49,684
So, why not use Penguin
to lead you to them?

443
00:24:50,155 --> 00:24:52,124
If I could figure out
how to do that, I would.

444
00:24:54,793 --> 00:24:56,284
It was good to
see you, Detective.

445
00:24:56,829 --> 00:24:58,627
You should come by
the house for dinner.

446
00:24:59,865 --> 00:25:00,865
Yes.

447
00:25:02,134 --> 00:25:03,134
I'd like that.

448
00:25:04,036 --> 00:25:06,028
How about we grab a bite...

449
00:25:08,974 --> 00:25:09,974
Tonight.

450
00:25:13,212 --> 00:25:15,147
Exclusive but welcoming.

451
00:25:15,214 --> 00:25:17,513
Urbane and edgy.

452
00:25:17,883 --> 00:25:19,374
Tonight's opening

453
00:25:19,485 --> 00:25:21,351
will establish the
Iceberg Lounge

454
00:25:21,420 --> 00:25:23,150
as Gotham's newest place to see,

455
00:25:23,889 --> 00:25:24,889
and be seen.

456
00:25:24,990 --> 00:25:27,030
And you say you acquired
the club from Barbara Kean?

457
00:25:27,226 --> 00:25:28,694
Is that a question?

458
00:25:29,328 --> 00:25:31,006
It's just no one's seen
her for months, and...

459
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:32,498
Barbara Kean's whereabouts

460
00:25:32,564 --> 00:25:33,759
are not my concern.

461
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:37,200
This was The Sirens
club. It is now mine.

462
00:25:37,603 --> 00:25:38,603
MAN: Mr. Cobblepot,

463
00:25:38,771 --> 00:25:41,371
there's a rumor going around
about criminals being given licenses.

464
00:25:41,573 --> 00:25:42,905
The rumor is
you're issuing them.

465
00:25:43,709 --> 00:25:45,974
Tell me, what is the
crime rate in Gotham?

466
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:47,808
We're at historic lows.

467
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:49,309
Historic lows...

468
00:25:51,383 --> 00:25:54,376
You know, Augustus
Caesar once presided

469
00:25:54,486 --> 00:25:58,719
over the longest period of peace and
prosperity the world has ever known.

470
00:25:59,525 --> 00:26:01,050
It was called the Pax Romana.

471
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:05,660
Perhaps one day, this will be
known as the Pax Penguina.

472
00:26:06,365 --> 00:26:07,890
That's not a denial.

473
00:26:08,901 --> 00:26:10,733
We're here to
talk about my club.

474
00:26:12,438 --> 00:26:14,464
Your readers will find
this interesting. Ivy?

475
00:26:15,374 --> 00:26:16,374
(REMOTE BEEPS)

476
00:26:16,942 --> 00:26:18,103
(CAMERAS CLICKING)

477
00:26:18,977 --> 00:26:20,468
That's Edward Nygma.

478
00:26:22,114 --> 00:26:24,310
Turns out, Ed had a
very rare brain disease,

479
00:26:24,883 --> 00:26:26,083
and there was only one option,

480
00:26:26,151 --> 00:26:27,881
to freeze him and
wait for the cure.

481
00:26:29,988 --> 00:26:31,479
In his final lucid moments,

482
00:26:32,758 --> 00:26:36,786
he begged me, "Oswald,
do not hide me away.

483
00:26:37,396 --> 00:26:38,659
"Put me out with the people."

484
00:26:41,467 --> 00:26:42,594
It was the least I could do.

485
00:26:43,168 --> 00:26:45,069
Anyone tell him he
was being frozen?

486
00:26:46,638 --> 00:26:49,301
I have affidavits from his doctor
if you would like to see them.

487
00:26:49,408 --> 00:26:50,408
No, thanks.

488
00:26:56,949 --> 00:26:57,949
Well, Jim.

489
00:26:58,317 --> 00:27:00,980
I'm rather busy, so
whatever your business is...

490
00:27:01,086 --> 00:27:02,952
I came to tell
you you're a fraud.

491
00:27:03,455 --> 00:27:06,323
The gang that has
Crane's fear toxin,

492
00:27:06,425 --> 00:27:07,465
they're not afraid of you.

493
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:10,561
Others will find out.
That's how it begins.

494
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:15,131
You've had a nice run,
Oswald, but it's over.

495
00:27:17,102 --> 00:27:20,436
Oh, Jim, it's so hard to admit
when you've become irrelevant.

496
00:27:23,375 --> 00:27:25,003
Let me tell you
what's gonna happen.

497
00:27:25,811 --> 00:27:26,972
I'm going to find this gang

498
00:27:27,646 --> 00:27:28,773
and I'm going to crush them.

499
00:27:29,548 --> 00:27:32,643
And everyone will see
that it is Oswald Cobblepot,

500
00:27:33,118 --> 00:27:35,110
the Penguin, who
keeps Gotham safe.

501
00:27:38,323 --> 00:27:39,951
Always good to
see you, old friend.

502
00:27:40,859 --> 00:27:44,489
<i>As he prepares for the
opening of the Iceberg Lounge,</i>

503
00:27:44,663 --> 00:27:47,656
<i>Oswald Cobblepot announced
that he would destroy the gang</i>

504
00:27:47,766 --> 00:27:51,464
<i>that attacked Gotham First
National Bank yesterday.</i>

505
00:27:51,803 --> 00:27:52,803
<i>He described them as</i>

506
00:27:52,871 --> 00:27:54,464
<i>cowards and pond scum.</i>

507
00:27:54,540 --> 00:27:55,701
(SIGHS)

508
00:27:56,875 --> 00:27:58,867
Penguin's goin' down tonight.

509
00:28:02,981 --> 00:28:04,711
- You finish that new batch yet?
- Yes.

510
00:28:05,651 --> 00:28:08,519
Now, can you please... Can
you please get rid of that, please?

511
00:28:09,621 --> 00:28:12,557
- What, you and him ain't gettin' along?
- Please, just get rid of it.

512
00:28:13,292 --> 00:28:15,557
Listen, I got to do
some things tonight,

513
00:28:16,028 --> 00:28:18,429
but I think you guys should
spend some time together. Huh?

514
00:28:19,364 --> 00:28:21,560
We all have our fears to face.

515
00:28:21,767 --> 00:28:22,928
(WHIMPERING)

516
00:28:23,035 --> 00:28:25,334
Stop! Stop! Please, stop!

517
00:28:25,404 --> 00:28:26,929
Please! No!

518
00:28:27,873 --> 00:28:28,873
Stop!

519
00:28:29,374 --> 00:28:30,899
(BANGING ON DOOR)

520
00:28:31,443 --> 00:28:32,672
Let me out!

521
00:28:37,182 --> 00:28:39,674
Remember how you accused me
of being a slave to my emotions?

522
00:28:40,786 --> 00:28:41,786
No more.

523
00:28:42,554 --> 00:28:43,920
I have banished those feelings.

524
00:28:45,357 --> 00:28:46,518
And look how I have risen.

525
00:28:49,494 --> 00:28:50,494
But at what cost?

526
00:28:52,030 --> 00:28:53,362
I wonder which of us is frozen.

527
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:56,000
Him.

528
00:28:57,202 --> 00:28:58,727
He's, like, totally frozen.

529
00:29:00,105 --> 00:29:02,438
Ivy, go somewhere else.

530
00:29:11,883 --> 00:29:12,883
All right,

531
00:29:13,585 --> 00:29:15,349
I want two unmarked
units at street level

532
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:18,420
and another two teams with me and
Harvey watching the entrances to the club.

533
00:29:18,890 --> 00:29:20,415
The moment that
gang arrives, we move.

534
00:29:23,795 --> 00:29:26,492
You heard the
man! Suit up, let's go!

535
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:32,794
Can we count on them?

536
00:29:32,904 --> 00:29:35,965
Let's see. You tricked Penguin
into baiting the gang to attack his club

537
00:29:36,074 --> 00:29:38,475
hoping to arrest them
before they cause mass panic

538
00:29:38,777 --> 00:29:41,838
only so you could embarrass Penguin.
So I would say, yeah, they're about as

539
00:29:42,014 --> 00:29:44,058
dependable as any other
part of this cockamamie plan.

540
00:29:44,082 --> 00:29:46,244
Thanks, I'll get the gas masks.

541
00:30:00,966 --> 00:30:02,662
Please, let me out!

542
00:30:05,137 --> 00:30:06,137
SCARECROW: <i>Jonathan.</i>

543
00:30:13,979 --> 00:30:14,979
Let me out!

544
00:30:16,415 --> 00:30:17,415
SCARECROW: <i>Jonathan!</i>

545
00:30:18,483 --> 00:30:19,815
(ROARING)

546
00:30:32,964 --> 00:30:35,627
- So, you guys work for Penguin, huh?
- It ain't like that.

547
00:30:36,068 --> 00:30:37,696
- Sure.
- Come on, Gordon.

548
00:30:37,903 --> 00:30:40,463
Since Penguin's been
cracking down, life's been good.

549
00:30:40,539 --> 00:30:41,666
Why you gotta rock the boat?

550
00:30:44,042 --> 00:30:46,409
What happens when he starts
giving out licenses for murders?

551
00:30:47,713 --> 00:30:49,511
Huh? What then?

552
00:30:50,582 --> 00:30:52,744
- I'm wasting my breath, aren't I?
- Pretty much.

553
00:30:55,721 --> 00:30:56,721
All right, then.

554
00:30:58,690 --> 00:30:59,690
Who wants it first?

555
00:31:07,666 --> 00:31:09,532
(JAZZY MUSIC PLAYING)

556
00:31:11,002 --> 00:31:12,800
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

557
00:31:15,307 --> 00:31:17,538
Mr. Wayne. Mr. Pennyworth.

558
00:31:18,009 --> 00:31:20,535
- I am so glad you could make it.
- It's our pleasure.

559
00:31:21,480 --> 00:31:22,480
Congratulations.

560
00:31:23,515 --> 00:31:25,507
We were just admiring
your frozen mate.

561
00:31:27,119 --> 00:31:28,280
Is he still alive in there?

562
00:31:29,087 --> 00:31:30,453
I fear we may never know.

563
00:31:31,123 --> 00:31:32,923
But you'll know when
you finally thaw him out,

564
00:31:33,592 --> 00:31:35,561
when they discover
a cure for his disease.

565
00:31:35,627 --> 00:31:38,563
Oh, yes, then, of course.

566
00:31:39,264 --> 00:31:40,341
I wanted to personally thank you

567
00:31:40,365 --> 00:31:41,965
for everything you've
done for this city.

568
00:31:42,868 --> 00:31:43,961
Thank you, Mr. Wayne.

569
00:31:45,404 --> 00:31:46,404
So...

570
00:31:47,639 --> 00:31:49,073
Can I ask about the licenses?

571
00:31:50,208 --> 00:31:52,053
A little discretion, if you
would, Master Bruce?

572
00:31:52,077 --> 00:31:53,221
Everybody's talking
about it, Alfred,

573
00:31:53,245 --> 00:31:54,565
I just want to
know how it works.

574
00:31:56,081 --> 00:31:57,572
So, does someone
come to you and say,

575
00:31:58,683 --> 00:31:59,683
"I want to rob a bank"?

576
00:32:01,787 --> 00:32:03,449
Now, Bruce, if I
didn't know any better,

577
00:32:03,555 --> 00:32:05,635
I would think that you
wanted me to implicate myself.

578
00:32:05,957 --> 00:32:07,516
Anything you say
stays between us.

579
00:32:09,961 --> 00:32:11,054
First, let me ask,

580
00:32:11,863 --> 00:32:15,300
you would be agreeable to
the idea of licensed crime?

581
00:32:15,734 --> 00:32:18,067
If crime had been licensed
and controlled three years ago,

582
00:32:18,136 --> 00:32:19,434
my parents would still be alive.

583
00:32:21,072 --> 00:32:22,072
Exactly so.

584
00:32:24,209 --> 00:32:25,575
Well, between us,

585
00:32:26,378 --> 00:32:28,813
I have nothing to do
with the licenses directly.

586
00:32:29,147 --> 00:32:32,311
I provide the guidelines
while Mr. Penn

587
00:32:32,784 --> 00:32:34,150
handles all of the details.

588
00:32:36,621 --> 00:32:38,487
Now, would you excuse me?

589
00:32:43,829 --> 00:32:45,422
- Well done, sir.
- Thank you.

590
00:32:46,531 --> 00:32:47,692
Now we know who has the list.

591
00:32:48,967 --> 00:32:49,967
The next step is...

592
00:32:52,170 --> 00:32:53,170
Selina.

593
00:33:02,481 --> 00:33:03,481
Where's your babysitter?

594
00:33:05,250 --> 00:33:07,185
It's kind of a package deal.

595
00:33:07,285 --> 00:33:08,617
Yeah, well, he's got me.

596
00:33:09,688 --> 00:33:10,951
Is that good enough or not?

597
00:33:11,423 --> 00:33:14,416
Actually, we're both in.

598
00:33:18,263 --> 00:33:21,324
- I should pat you down for weapons.
- Sure.

599
00:33:21,633 --> 00:33:24,933
- If you wanna lose a hand.
- It was worth a shot.

600
00:33:26,037 --> 00:33:27,037
I'll tell the boss.

601
00:33:29,307 --> 00:33:30,307
See ya.

602
00:33:36,715 --> 00:33:38,183
You were worried about me.

603
00:33:46,491 --> 00:33:47,550
(DOOR OPENS)

604
00:33:47,926 --> 00:33:50,088
Hey, man, I've been
looking all over for you.

605
00:33:51,196 --> 00:33:52,255
Ooh, ouch.

606
00:33:53,098 --> 00:33:54,430
Think we can
forget about backup.

607
00:33:55,367 --> 00:33:57,393
I see you talked to some
of your fellow officers.

608
00:33:58,169 --> 00:34:00,001
- Probably not a bad thing.
- How's that?

609
00:34:00,305 --> 00:34:03,366
Guys get to let off steam,
resentments don't fester.

610
00:34:03,875 --> 00:34:05,707
Next time, you can
get punched in the face.

611
00:34:05,810 --> 00:34:07,676
This beautiful mug,
no one would dare.

612
00:34:08,013 --> 00:34:09,013
Let's go.

613
00:34:16,555 --> 00:34:20,048
All right, once inside, get
Zsasz and Penguin first,

614
00:34:20,158 --> 00:34:21,217
and then go crazy.

615
00:34:21,493 --> 00:34:22,722
I still don't see Penguin.

616
00:34:23,695 --> 00:34:24,695
PENGUIN: Hello!

617
00:34:25,764 --> 00:34:29,201
I'm guessing that gas isn't faster
than a bullet, what do you think?

618
00:34:32,237 --> 00:34:34,797
Jim Gordon and his
ham-fisted manipulation.

619
00:34:36,274 --> 00:34:37,274
He thought he fooled me.

620
00:34:37,475 --> 00:34:39,307
You wanna do 'em
here or downstairs?

621
00:34:39,744 --> 00:34:41,610
- Might be a little loud in here.
- Neither.

622
00:34:44,249 --> 00:34:46,582
I have something
special planned for them.

623
00:35:02,601 --> 00:35:03,625
What do you want, Bruce?

624
00:35:06,137 --> 00:35:07,137
You knew I'd follow you.

625
00:35:07,973 --> 00:35:09,441
Just like I knew
you'd come up here.

626
00:35:10,709 --> 00:35:12,109
You don't know
anything about me.

627
00:35:15,714 --> 00:35:17,794
I wanted to apologize for
what I said at the hospital

628
00:35:17,882 --> 00:35:19,111
when you came to visit Alfred.

629
00:35:20,485 --> 00:35:21,783
You were making a kind gesture.

630
00:35:26,925 --> 00:35:28,450
You wanna talk to
me, come up here.

631
00:35:41,373 --> 00:35:42,466
My point is, I'm sorry.

632
00:35:45,944 --> 00:35:49,039
Yeah, you were a jerk.

633
00:35:53,952 --> 00:35:55,511
I saw you arrive
with Tabitha Galavan.

634
00:35:58,023 --> 00:35:59,651
I'm not sure I'd
choose her as a mentor.

635
00:35:59,891 --> 00:36:00,891
Wow.

636
00:36:03,328 --> 00:36:04,990
That means absolutely
nothing to me.

637
00:36:12,437 --> 00:36:13,437
Selina...

638
00:36:14,973 --> 00:36:15,973
Oh?

639
00:36:17,509 --> 00:36:19,341
You wanna say something?

640
00:36:24,382 --> 00:36:26,062
It's a lovely dress
you're wearing tonight.

641
00:36:26,551 --> 00:36:28,042
(APPROACHING FOOTSTEPS)

642
00:36:29,054 --> 00:36:30,113
Honestly, you two,

643
00:36:30,522 --> 00:36:33,219
why can't you just go to the
cinema like normal teenagers?

644
00:36:33,825 --> 00:36:37,421
And, Master Bruce, we got a
bit of a situation downstairs, sir.

645
00:36:38,863 --> 00:36:39,863
What sort of situation?

646
00:36:42,434 --> 00:36:43,434
Ms. Kyle.

647
00:36:49,574 --> 00:36:51,941
PENGUIN: For the past three
months, I have given this city

648
00:36:52,277 --> 00:36:54,007
a tranquility it
has never known.

649
00:36:54,713 --> 00:36:57,945
Now, I would like to ensure
that peace for the future.

650
00:36:59,117 --> 00:37:00,117
In the weeks to come,

651
00:37:00,518 --> 00:37:01,952
you will hear whispers

652
00:37:02,053 --> 00:37:04,079
about what's happening
on the streets of Gotham.

653
00:37:04,422 --> 00:37:06,084
All you need to know is

654
00:37:06,357 --> 00:37:09,919
without me, this
is what you get.

655
00:37:10,061 --> 00:37:13,554
Men who want to bring
fear back to our city.

656
00:37:13,765 --> 00:37:16,860
Who promise a
return to the old days.

657
00:37:17,068 --> 00:37:19,503
So, tell your families,

658
00:37:20,071 --> 00:37:21,266
tell your friends,

659
00:37:21,673 --> 00:37:25,610
it is Oswald Cobblepot
who keeps them safe.

660
00:37:26,077 --> 00:37:28,069
Not the GCPD.

661
00:37:31,349 --> 00:37:32,349
You're welcome.

662
00:37:38,289 --> 00:37:40,367
I have my things in the car, we
can stop them in the parking garage.

663
00:37:40,391 --> 00:37:41,916
Absolutely not, Master Bruce.

664
00:37:42,427 --> 00:37:44,572
Alfred, Penguin's gonna take
those men out and kill them.

665
00:37:44,596 --> 00:37:45,596
Undoubtedly so.

666
00:37:46,297 --> 00:37:48,297
But, as you said before,
you can make a difference.

667
00:37:49,400 --> 00:37:52,564
There is time for masks, and
there is a time for Bruce Wayne.

668
00:37:54,005 --> 00:37:55,649
PENGUIN: Do you know
what's going to be done to you?

669
00:37:55,673 --> 00:37:56,673
Wait!

670
00:37:58,343 --> 00:38:00,343
I want to know what you're
gonna do with those men.

671
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:02,740
You need not concern
yourself with that.

672
00:38:02,814 --> 00:38:04,658
Are those men going to
be turned over to the police?

673
00:38:04,682 --> 00:38:05,741
(CHUCKLES)

674
00:38:10,989 --> 00:38:13,982
Earlier tonight, you thanked
me for making the city safer.

675
00:38:14,726 --> 00:38:16,217
Now, how do you
think that happened?

676
00:38:17,095 --> 00:38:19,621
I do the dirty work
no one else will.

677
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:22,800
I understand.

678
00:38:23,735 --> 00:38:26,068
But I'm asking you, turn
those men over to the police.

679
00:38:28,339 --> 00:38:29,339
You're young.

680
00:38:31,943 --> 00:38:32,943
You have a good heart.

681
00:38:37,415 --> 00:38:38,415
No.

682
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:44,455
Enjoy your party, Penguin.

683
00:38:44,889 --> 00:38:45,889
You little twerp.

684
00:38:46,891 --> 00:38:48,291
(PEOPLE GASPING)

685
00:38:51,963 --> 00:38:54,398
- (GUN COCKING)
- (GRUNTS)

686
00:39:01,706 --> 00:39:02,901
(SCREAMS)

687
00:39:06,544 --> 00:39:08,137
(GASPING)

688
00:39:11,416 --> 00:39:12,440
(DISTORTED) What's wrong?

689
00:39:12,717 --> 00:39:13,717
You scared?

690
00:39:14,018 --> 00:39:15,018
(SCREAMING)

691
00:39:15,286 --> 00:39:16,982
(DISTORTED LAUGHTER)

692
00:39:17,622 --> 00:39:18,715
(SCREAMING)

693
00:39:19,724 --> 00:39:21,886
(GRUNTING)

694
00:39:24,162 --> 00:39:25,162
No!

695
00:39:25,230 --> 00:39:26,323
(LAUGHING)

696
00:39:28,366 --> 00:39:29,366
GORDON: Hey!

697
00:39:29,801 --> 00:39:30,962
(THUDS)

698
00:39:32,570 --> 00:39:33,570
You're under arrest.

699
00:39:34,005 --> 00:39:36,736
By order of the Gotham City
Police Department. Cuff him.

700
00:39:36,841 --> 00:39:38,241
(PENGUIN GASPS)

701
00:39:42,013 --> 00:39:44,005
(GASPING)

702
00:39:44,349 --> 00:39:46,250
Help me. Help me.

703
00:39:46,751 --> 00:39:49,448
(SOBBING)

704
00:39:52,457 --> 00:39:54,057
HARVEY: Penguin
ain't gonna be too happy.

705
00:39:56,261 --> 00:39:57,261
Screw him.

706
00:39:58,696 --> 00:40:00,496
I'm just worried about
finding Jonathan Crane.

707
00:40:00,698 --> 00:40:03,099
If he's out there with access
to his father's formula...

708
00:40:03,201 --> 00:40:04,794
Relax, we'll find him.

709
00:40:05,370 --> 00:40:07,530
Wouldn't expect too much
help from these parts, though.

710
00:40:07,605 --> 00:40:08,971
There's good cops out there.

711
00:40:09,641 --> 00:40:10,641
They just need reminding.

712
00:40:12,577 --> 00:40:15,513
(CARS HONKING)

713
00:40:28,726 --> 00:40:29,726
BRUCE: You have a list

714
00:40:30,628 --> 00:40:33,063
of all the licenses
you've given. I want it.

715
00:40:33,598 --> 00:40:35,726
I... I can't.

716
00:40:38,369 --> 00:40:39,369
Penguin, he'll...

717
00:40:41,606 --> 00:40:42,606
(GASPS)

718
00:40:45,610 --> 00:40:46,908
(EXHALES SHAKILY)

719
00:41:09,367 --> 00:41:10,767
(GLASS SHATTERS IN DISTANCE)

720
00:41:12,670 --> 00:41:14,002
(OBJECTS CLATTERING)

721
00:41:14,539 --> 00:41:16,804
(ALARM RINGING)

722
00:41:17,108 --> 00:41:18,908
MAN 1: What about the
alarm? MAN 2: Forget it.

723
00:41:19,010 --> 00:41:20,569
We got a license, remember?

724
00:41:22,347 --> 00:41:23,610
(GLASS SHATTERS)

725
00:41:27,652 --> 00:41:29,621
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

726
00:41:29,954 --> 00:41:31,252
(GLASS CRACKLING)

727
00:41:31,689 --> 00:41:32,689
Oh, no.

728
00:41:34,859 --> 00:41:35,859
What the...

729
00:41:40,365 --> 00:41:41,365
(DOOR CRASHES)

730
00:41:41,466 --> 00:41:42,466
OFFICER: GCPD.

731
00:41:44,002 --> 00:41:45,493
Gotham Police,
you're under arrest.

732
00:41:48,039 --> 00:41:49,871
Crane, you got to make
more of that fear gas.

733
00:41:50,141 --> 00:41:51,473
We got to get
Merton out of jail.

734
00:41:51,743 --> 00:41:52,743
Crane!

735
00:41:57,682 --> 00:41:58,682
Crane?

736
00:42:03,087 --> 00:42:05,352
(DISTORTED) Jonathan
Crane isn't here anymore.

737
00:42:07,191 --> 00:42:08,523
(GROWLS SOFTLY)

738
00:42:10,728 --> 00:42:12,026
It's just the Scarecrow.

739
00:42:13,231 --> 00:42:15,063
(SCREAMING)

740
00:42:16,734 --> 00:42:19,067
(ROARING)

741
00:43:00,578 --> 00:43:01,578
English - SDH
